# APP-SPLIT-003F — gates log (2026-11-27)

Lane: pure-move extraction of the audio capture & scoring wiring slice from
App() into apps/desktop/src/app/capture-wiring.ts as `useCaptureWiring(deps)`.
App.tsx keeps owning every useState hook, all slice state and the render;
the hook owns the slice's two refs (captureOwner, captureRouteRef), its two
device-release effects and the handler bodies. Call-site names arrive by
destructuring — zero JSX/handler edits.

## Measurement + slice pick (card method step 1)

Measured from HEAD (0150f827/dee0af3b, App.tsx 4526 lines) with
`grep -nE '^\s*(async function|function) ' apps/desktop/src/App.tsx` and
the JSX-return structure (`return (` at 3631). Largest cohesive wiring
blocks left inline, by distance between consecutive top-level functions:

- audio capture & scoring (playBlobUrl .. stopAndCheck + the two
  captureOwner release effects): lines 2844-3404 = **561 lines** — the mic
  capture owner, the pronunciation/dictation/free-speaking/free-writing
  openers, prompt fetches, graded submits and the four analyze* scorers.
- story/reading + my-words handlers (2258-2677): ~420 lines — REJECTED:
  exactly the region ARCH-HOTSPOT-2026-11-27 was actively editing
  (playSentenceClip refactor) at lane start; extracting there would collide
  with a live sibling lane.
- scenario surface (2678-2846): ~170 lines.
- placement + kanji handlers (~1945-2140): ~195 lines.
- navigate/history effects (~3399 region post-move) + remaining JSX
  surfaces: smaller fragments; JSX surfaces need component extraction
  (bigger contract than one card's pure-move budget).

Pick: audio capture & scoring — the single largest cohesive slice, one
closed dependency group (its internals call each other; outside App it is
touched only by name at JSX/click sites), and disjoint from every other
lane's in-flight edits.

